     [{:path "specs/cli-workflow/tasks.md",
       :marker "cli-implementation-tasks",
       :id
       "cli/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-checkruncompilebuildtestpackageverify-to-real-services",
       :before
       "Executed success/failure fixtures and artifact paths at public command boundary T1 acceptance: actual command execution records and artifact paths/manifest hashes retain declared grants/denials. Reject ungranted effects, silent unsafe/AI/network/shell/secrets/publish operations, hidden network, output-directory escape without grant and missing release artifact verification. Foundation requirement gravity/hosted-hello-execution: Compile the D2 hosted hello source through actual Reader, Syntax, macro expansion and hosted execution, preserving stage/source identities and recording the declared stdout effect and granted authority with the produced output. Refusals: Reject malformed source and the same program without stdout authority; a static hello manifest, host-language print or supplied output string cannot establish execution. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence. Release extension release/public-check-command: Through the public gravity executable, check declared hello, core and nontrivial applications for both .qst and .gravity. Retain expected check results/artifacts, exact source path/extension, executable/compiler identity and normalized command stdout/stderr. Internal calls or relabelled extensions are not public command evidence. Reject missing parity with P18T04001 and invalid inputs with owning diagnostics. Release extension release/public-run-command: Run each declared hello/core/nontrivial application through public gravity under its declared runtime/grants for both canonical extensions; compare actual output/exit with fixture expectations. Preserve supplied source path/kind and normalized transcripts. Reject missing public execution, incorrect output or hidden delegated runtime failure; manifest presence and internal evaluator results do not establish public run. Release extension release/public-compile-output-command: Execute gravity compile for declared hello/core/nontrivial applications in both canonical extensions, including requested -o locations. Retain actual executable outputs/hashes, sidecars/provenance, compiler identity and original source paths/extensions. Reject missing/substituted executable, ignored output location, invalid target, provenance mismatch and command parity failure; supplied candidate records alone are not compilation. Release extension release/generated-application-execution: Invoke the exact artifacts emitted by public compile, including the declared core-app executable, and compare hello/core/nontrivial outputs/exits under declared runtime or no-runtime boundaries. Bind execution to emitted hashes and original provenance for both extensions. Reject missing, substituted, non-executable or behaviorally wrong outputs; successful compilation cannot replace generated-application execution. Release extension release/public-rejection-diagnostics: Exercise parser, semantic/arity, capability, package and release invalid applications through the same public executable. Preserve owning stable code, applicable span/manifest/profile/source context, non-success exit and normalized stdout/stderr; prove paired extension/path rejection parity. Include applicable L1-DELIMITER, L2-FUNCTION-ARITY, P4-HOST-CAPABILITY, PKG10001 and B13-RELEASE cases. Reject swallowed failure, generic substituted categories and invalid success. Release extension release/public-subset-test-bridge: Exercise gravity test's bootstrap-hosted current-public-subset bridge through accepted check/run/compile/generated-execution and rejected stable-diagnostic cases, retaining source paths and both canonical extensions. Proof names actual subset and hosting. Reject test --full and full-language/self-hosted-runner overclaims with P18T04006. Retain this bounded surface separately from final self-hosted full-language conformance. Release extension release/public-incomplete-selfhost-verifier: While final seed retirement or release is incomplete, public gravity self-host verify writes an honest incomplete proof with active compiler source path/extension and seed facts, then fails closed with P18T04007. Invalid self-host invocation rejects with P18T04008. Exercise both through the public boundary. Incomplete proof production or hosted command availability cannot establish final successful self-host verification."}
