       "Version/profile/target and artifact IDs present? Missing/stale stages shown honestly? Check-elision evidence visible? [IR inspector](../../docs/phase-13-tooling-and-developer-experience/186-t10-compiler-explorer-and-ir-inspector-design.md) Verify every T10 stage with compiler/project/profile/target/stage identity, available semantic facts, upstream/source/generated-origin edges, pass input/output and target assumptions. Export IR JSON, diff/preservation/source-map/redacted bundles; reject missing context, lost origins, secret exports and check removal without preservation evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/tooling-semantic-consistency: Make formatter/LSP/REPL/inspection consumers use actual compiler diagnostics, syntax/source identities and compiled profile/effect/capability boundaries; compare supported tool and ordinary compiler results on the same accepted and rejected inputs. Refusals: Reject stale tool diagnostics, lost syntax identity, a refactor changing source meaning or interactive evaluation bypassing compiled grant/profile checks; no alternate tool-only language semantics. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products; diag/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/integrate-runtimebuildeditor-consumers-without-rule-drift - Actual runtime/compiler/tool structured diagnostics with stable owning codes and provenance; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products."}],
