onformance - Exact component/slice contracts, declared unsupported scope and claimed-support evidence. Foundation requirement gravity/domain-concept-layer-map: Publish a domain-concept map relating each declared concept to its source forms, Core/domain IR boundary, emitted artifact, effects and required capabilities; verify a representative domain product against that map. Refusals: Reject an unmapped claimed concept, a host API substituted for its source meaning or a mapping that treats an effect declaration as a capability grant. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): pipeline - Versioned stage contracts and actual compiler stage/fact/origin products. Foundation requirement gravity/qualify-ambiguous-normative-terms: For normative uses whose meaning affects implementation, require an explicit qualified D3 concept or owning contract reference; report the exact ambiguous span and the competing interpretations. Refusals: Reject unqualified uses such as runtime/profile/target or effect/capability where they change the required implementation meaning; ordinary nonnormative prose does not create a new terminology gate. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion."}],
