     :required-output
     "Identify and bind the actual producer, checker or consumer task, criteria, dependencies and source evidence for: Actually invoke an admitted compiler/tool plugin or pass on its declared typed syntax/core/MIR/domain-IR/schema input and obtain its declared transformed artifact/result with source and actual execution provenance. Consume published pass contracts and current load/authority/output-verifier results; ordinary generated-program checking remains at the existing shared gate.",
     :scope
     "Exact required-output criterion allocation only; no whole-attached-facet proof or implementation acceptance.",
     :status :open,
     :kind :existing-current-criterion-witness-proposal,
     :independent-current-allocation-review :pending,
     :proposed-joined-binding nil,
     :criterion
     "| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Check manifest compatibility before code loading | Actual loader validates package identity, API/compiler version, declared passes/artifacts, trust and grants; incompatible/malformed/rejected packages produce diagnostics without executing initialization code. |\n| Execute scoped plugin context | Run a deterministic read-only analysis and authorized transformation through actual scoped IR APIs; read-only writes, unauthorized namespaces/phases and hidden compiler mutation reject at the operation boundary. |\n| Enforce real sandbox/build-effect boundaries | Exercise sandboxed and policy-trusted plugin execution; filesystem/network/process/environment/model/tool/artifact operations without grants are denied before effects, including host escape paths. Trust labels alone do not disable scoped checks. |\n| Register passes, facets and domain interfaces | Require declared schema, verifier, profile support, effects, lowering path and conformance records as applicable; execute registered schema/verifier callbacks and reject opaque, conflicting or unauthorized registration. Component owners retain domain semantics. |\n| Verify output, trace execution and revalidate reuse | Run the declared output verifier, reject invalid transformed artifacts, record actual plugin/package/grant/input/output/replay identities, and invalidate cache entries on changed versions, policy or dependencies. |",
     :implementation-acceptance :unassessed,
     :canonical-adoption :pending},
