      {:path
       "docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/115-r4-managed-runtime-design.md",
       :raw-sha256
       "829089155b7d61a613ccf82c10ee9e85813b208502aa1f27adc94b3c3693bb7f",
       :raw
       "- `R1`, `R5`, `R9`, `R10`, `R11`, and `R12` define shared runtime services,\n  memory, REPL, FFI, capabilities, and observability.\n",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "R4/source/2631f364bfb90ec9dc4eec6a2d87410fc9c6a39d010b804fc0eb1ebcc60f8573",
       :id "facet/runtime-domains-schema/r4/f922993e32714229a50a55e4",
       :kind :context,
       :document-id "R4",
       :end-byte 2296,
       :start-byte 2166}
      {:path
       "docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/116-r5-memory-runtime-design.md",
       :raw-sha256
       "06c6e30102f16b8338f9f5705f83cf858b75c99c3f8263d3a45e8918f7dd2320",
       :raw
       "Unsafe implementation internals may use raw pointers, platform allocators, or\ndevice APIs. Safe wrappers must state invariants, capability requirements,\nownership transfer, failure behavior, and proof obligations. Unsafe internals do\nnot make the safe API unsafe when the wrapper contract is verified.\n",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "R5/source/a35818e8f632ab73a757b1be06c46f4104608ce0feab1409e29d1f216615ccd7",
       :id "facet/runtime-domains-schema/r5/0be2acf218689d063d722ff1",
       :kind :condition,
       :document-id "R5",
       :end-byte 4079,
       :start-byte 3777}
      {:path
       "docs/phase-08-runtime-architecture/116-r5-memory-runtime-design.md",
       :raw-sha256
       "b65387fc7c691358a2e0e4b3b227d2a916568c806746878b07fa840582256416",
       :raw
       "- Raw memory is unavailable to safe code except through audited unsafe islands or\n  safe wrappers with proven invariants.\n",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "R5/source/0c3fd611d2ed4dbbd2ebe174352e3e15bc3b6c1190b8fd5a5bc6cec6c7b8b952",
       :id "facet/runtime-domains-schema/r5/1e97340d5732b2888ae974ae",
       :kind :condition,
       :document-id "R5",
